                <pb facs="0282" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg214"/>

                <head>B.</head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Reply of the Emperor.</hi>
                </p>
                <p>I thank you, general, for the sentiments you have expressed to me in the name of
                    the government of the United States. The historical recollections to which you
                    have referred are a sure guarantee that no misunderstanding will disturb the
                    friendly relations which have so long existed between France and the American
                    Union. Á loyal and sincere understanding will, I do not doubt, contribute to the
                    interest of industry and commerce, which are every day astonishing the world by
                    their prodigies, and will insure the progress of civilization. Your presence
                    among us cannot fail to contribute to this happy result by maintaining relations
                    to which I attach the greatest value.</p>
            </div>
